    "AI Notes": {
      "value": "SUPERFLEX is a Danish artist collective founded in 1993 by Jakob Fenger, Bj\u00f8rnstjerne Christiansen, and Rasmus Rosengren Nielsen; based in Copenhagen. Highly senior: over 30 years of self-directed practice, represented by galleries in Madrid, Seoul, Basel, LA, and Mexico City; works in MoMA, Tate Modern, Louisiana Museum, Hirshhorn, and many others. Their practice spans large-scale public art (Superkilen, 2011, with BIG + Topotek1), video and film (Flooded McDonald's, Modern Times Forever), installations, social/economic propositions (Free Beer, Guaran\u00e1 Power), and participatory performance. Recipients of the Mies van der Rohe Prize nomination (2013), Civic Trust Award (2013), George Maciunas Award (2009). LinkedIn lists 11-50 employees; About page names 7 staff including a Head of Production and Head of Projects. Autonomy 5: fully self-directed collective, no employer, long institutional track record. Work Status: Studio confirmed by studio address, gallery representation, and institutional profile.",
      "source_url": null,
      "verified_at": "2026-07-13T10:15:59",
      "set_by": "agent"
    },
